  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5fca8c79aca10c0069e36e33",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/64bf6f26854d620d318d4082f2e6a6a7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FE-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/64bf6f26854d620d318d4082f2e6a6a7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FE-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/64bf6f26854d620d318d4082f2e6a6a7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FE-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/64bf6f26854d620d318d4082f2e6a6a7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FE-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "eddie",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8c79aca10c0069e36e33",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This is pretty bad. Without actually looking at the code, I can guess what's happening: the DateUtility method for parsing a datetime string returns null if it can't parse the date. If the caller isn't checking for that and simply passing the returned value the situation described could result.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "So, either, check for null return, or, consider actually making the DateUtility method throw an exception (unchecked, maybe illegalargumentexception) but I'm not sure what else that would affect.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "For FCREPO-689, I already started some work on parsing datetime strings as rest params and returning 400 errors if there's a date parse error. I only needed it to handle lastModifiedDate, but I can apply it to all the REST params that take datetimes.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
     "created": "2010-05-24T19:26:41.738-0300",
