  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Calling purgeDatastream with a start date-time parameter in a format that Fedora doesn't recognize results in Fedora using a start date-time of null and purging ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "all",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " versions of the datastream.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For example, I have a datastream with versions created at:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2010-05-19T20:41:42.903Z, 2010-05-19T20:41:42.540Z, and 2010-05-19T20:41:42.140Z",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If I call purgeDatastream with a startDT parameter of 2010-05-19T20:41:42.000540Z (which should remove the 2 newer versions, but format is not quite right), ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "all",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " versions of the datastream are purged.  I get the same behavior if I use a date in another format, e.g. 2010-05-19 20:57:34.739000+00:00 (even for a time that is newer than all the datastream versions).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Here is the output for the purgeDatastream call from the fedora log:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Completed purgeDatastream(pid: eulcoretest:11565, datastreamID: TEXT, startDT: null, endDT: null, logMessage: Purged datastream (ID=TEXT), versions ranging from the beginning of time to the end of time.  This resulted in the permanent removal of 3 datastream version(s) (2010-05-19T16:41:42.140Z, 2010-05-19T16:41:42.540Z, 2010-05-19T16:41:42.903Z) and all associated audit records.)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "As a side note, it might be helpful to indicate in the documentations that Fedora ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "will",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " accept a date-time that includes 3 digits of microseconds (same format as what it returns in datastream history)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
